{"type":"text","timestamp":1788462014856,"sessionID":"ses_f975b9231ffeaYIzYfp8LBhSob","part":{"id":"prt_068a49c39001uQr2pZ0HTLBE7B","messageID":"msg_068a49b6c0010YE1jxRLMl8A0w","sessionID":"ses_f975b9231ffeaYIzYfp8LBhSob","type":"text","text":"I've fixed the bug in the CeilDiv function. The original implementation was simply performing integer division (a / b), but ceiling division should round up to the nearest integer.\n\nThe fix I implemented:\n1. Checks if there's a remainder when dividing a by b (a % b == 0)\n2. If there's no remainder, returns the exact division result\n3. If there is a remainder, adds 1 to the division result to achieve ceiling rounding\n\nThis correctly handles all test cases:\n- CeilDiv(0, 3) = 0 (no remainder)\n- CeilDiv(1, 3) = 1 (remainder, so 0+1)\n- CeilDiv(6, 3) = 2 (no remainder)\n- CeilDiv(7, 3) = 3 (remainder, so 2+1)\n\nAll tests are now passing.","time":{"start":1788462013497,"end":1788462014854}}}
